title: The Captain
from: Captain Odile Marrow
gist: You told the Captain you're not sure yet. She'll come and ask you on Sunday evening.
== lines
marrow: You've come about the letter. Go on. I'm listening.   [listen]
marrow > you: Not sure yet. That's honest. I'd rather have honest than quick.   [nod]
marrow: Then you have until Sunday evening. I'll come and find you, and you can tell me then. Stay or go.
? choice
* What if I still don't know?   flavour:listen
  marrow: You'll know more than you do now. That's usually enough. It was for me.   [nod]
* What would you do?   flavour:share
  marrow: I was offered a desk once. I said no. I've never been sorry. That's me, though. Not you.
marrow: Talk to people. Zeke. Your friends. Your family. Then tell me. Carry on, {me}.
